cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Seismic refraction data, terrain inputs, and calibration outputs for
  geophysics-informed critical-zone structure modeling at Dry Creek, Idaho
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or code, please cite both this archive and the
  associated paper.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Hang
    family-names: Chen
    affiliation: >-
      School of Earth, Environment, and Sustainability, University of Iowa
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-31"
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
abstract: >-
  Raw and processed seismic refraction records from seven P-wave profiles
  collected at the Treeline site, Dry Creek Experimental Watershed, Idaho,
  between May and September 2016, together with the terrain inputs, modeling
  and calibration source code, and SCE-UA calibration outputs used to constrain
  a reduced process-based model of critical-zone structure directly against
  first-arrival travel times. Includes SEG-2 shot gathers, merged SEG-Y line
  files, geophone coordinates, first-arrival picks in pyGIMLi unified format,
  digital elevation and flow-routing rasters, the full parameter search
  history, and the retained behavioral ensemble.
keywords:
  - critical zone
  - seismic refraction
  - rock physics
  - landscape evolution
  - Landlab
  - pyGIMLi
  - SCE-UA
  - Dry Creek Experimental Watershed
references:
